id: pm-zvy31w
title: Isolate CodSpeed dependency setup from unrelated Chrome APT index failures
description: "The benchmark runner inherits an unused Chrome APT source. PR 1225 run 34384419100 attempts 1 and 2 fail before benchmarks because its Packages.gz hash differs from the signed index. Preserve the source files but disable them in this disposable benchmark runner, retaining signature verification for Ubuntu dependencies."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-09T17:59:53.701Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-09T18:42:35.181Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-09T18:42:34.125Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-09T18:42:34.125Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Only unused Chrome sources disabled; Ubuntu sources and verification intact; present and absent fixtures plus workflow checks pass; hosted benchmarks execute and upload.
parent: pm-yh6t
severity: medium
resolution: Preserve and disable only unused Chrome sources; enforce four actual-step fixture populations and idempotence; narrow the script type explicitly for TypeScript and static analysis.
expected_result: "Signed Ubuntu dependencies and unrelated sources are retained, benchmark data uploads, and workflow regressions fail clearly."
actual_result: "Hosted 7dd3b run 34386816996 executed/uploaded 11 benchmarks. Final local guard correction passed 14 linked tests, ESLint and typecheck. Removed-step and widened-loop negative controls failed as intended. Hosted DeepScan recheck pending next push."
