comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-09T17:59:53.701Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: 84 all-status CodSpeed matches and zero exact Hash Sum mismatch matches. Full reads distinguish completed adoption pm-yh6t and completed cache fix pm-w16muu from this new Chrome index failure. Open and in-progress inventories checked."
  "2026-09-09T18:02:56.420Z","harness:codex","Verification: the actual YAML shell step passed disposable present-source, repeated-execution and absent-source fixtures. Both google-chrome.list and google-chrome.sources are preserved as disabled files; Ubuntu and an unrelated provider source retain identical bytes. Pinned actionlint 1.7.12 and ShellCheck passed, and the sandboxed workflow contract suite passed all 14 tests. The earlier full source suite passed 8639 tests with exact 100/100/100/100; this correction changes only CI YAML and PM/changelog data. Hosted benchmark acceptance remains pending for the correction push."
  "2026-09-09T18:25:42.538Z","harness:codex","Review follow-up: committed actual-step regression fixtures now cover absent, list-only, Deb822-only and both source formats, repeated execution, preserved bytes and unrelated Ubuntu/Microsoft sources. All 14 tests passed focused and linked; ESLint and typecheck passed. Two temporary workflow mutations (removed isolation step and widened file loop) each failed the test; original workflow restored exactly. Hosted run 34386816996 executed and uploaded all 11 benchmarks at 7dd3b7f6a; all 30 available checks passed, with 3 provider/expected skips. No application source changed after the exact 100/100/100/100 full-suite pass."
  "2026-09-09T18:42:33.174Z","harness:codex","DeepScan e1d0567 report 234366166 flagged the test cast because its dataflow model does not narrow through expect(...).toBeTypeOf. Replaced that assertion/cast with an explicit typeof guard and reused one steps array for existing lookups, preserving the ESLint complexity ceiling. All 14 linked workflow contract tests, ESLint and typecheck passed. No application-source changes; hosted DeepScan acceptance awaits the next push. Report: https://deepscan.io/dashboard/#view=project&pid=32092&iid=234366166"
